</Layout>

<style>
	/* ============================================================
	   Shared grid — ONE container for the whole page, matching the
	   header's own box exactly (var(--container):1016px + 24px
	   inline padding => content 968px, edges at 212/1228 on a 1440
	   viewport). Every section, table, card row and diagram sits
	   inside this same box; nothing else declares its own max-width.
	   ============================================================ */
	/* One reusable device-size system, used by every section that shows a
	   desktop/tablet/mobile screenshot (UI Design's Home Screen trio,
	   Prescription Flow's desktop+tablet pair). Chosen so the three fit
	   the standard grid (968px content) in the 3-up Home Screen row
	   while keeping the reference's desktop > tablet > mobile hierarchy:
	   424 + 280 + 210 + 2×27 gap = 968. Prescription's 2-up row reuses
	   the same desktop/tablet widths for consistency. */
	.oni {
		overflow-x: hidden;
		--case-desktop-w: 424px;
		--case-tablet-w: 280px;
		--case-mobile-w: 210px;
	}

	.block {
		max-width: var(--container);
		margin-inline: auto;
		padding: 76px 24px 0;
	}

	.split,
	.headrow {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: flex-start;
		gap: 40px;
		margin-bottom: 30px;
	}

	/* The repeated "large heading on one side + short supporting copy on
	   the other" pattern (My Role, Research to Design Principles, User
	   Journey, Competitive Landscape, UI Design, Validation…): the side
	   copy sits vertically centered against the heading block, not
	   pinned to its top. */
	.headrow--mid {
		align-items: center;
	}

	.headrow--tight {
		margin-bottom: 40px;
	}

	.headrow__side {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		max-width: 412px;
		text-align: left;
		font-size: 19px;
		line-height: 1.45;
